HOLLOW - pending wrapper patch: never dereference a null desktop capturer.

STATUS: NOT IN THE VENDORED BINARIES. lib/libwebrtc.so and lib/libwebrtc.dll
were built 2026-07-19, before this patch existed, so the app also carries a
plugin-side guard (common/cpp/src/flutter_screen_capture.cc skips capture types
the session cannot produce). Apply this at the next libwebrtc rebuild -
BUILDING.md step 2, next to hollow-screencast.patch - then fold it into that
file and delete this one.

WHY (issue #30, reported 2026-07-28 on Garuda KDE, reproduces on ANY Wayland
session): the wrapper calls capturer_->Start() straight after the factory with
no null check. libwebrtc m144 picks a Linux capturer like this
(modules/desktop_capture/{screen,window}_capturer_linux.cc):

  options.allow_pipewire() && wayland && pipewire loads -> BaseCapturerPipeWire
  !IsRunningUnderWayland()                              -> the X11 capturer
  otherwise                                             -> nullptr

The wrapper sets allow_pipewire for kScreen only, and the X11 fallback is
skipped outright under Wayland (XWayland running does not help). So a WINDOW
media list on Wayland always holds a null capturer, and opening the share
picker killed the app with SIGSEGV inside libwebrtc.so:

  #0 libwebrtc::RTCDesktopMediaListImpl::RTCDesktopMediaListImpl(...)::$_0
  #1 webrtc::Thread::Dispatch(...)   #2 ProcessMessages   #3 PreRun

This patch is null-safety only: a missing backend becomes an empty source list
and a CS_FAILED start instead of a crash. It deliberately does NOT enable
PipeWire for window capture - that works, but every media list that touches the
portal pops an xdg-desktop-portal dialog at picker-open time, so windows-on-
Wayland wants a portal-first picker (one entry, no thumbnails, restore token),
not a flag flip.

